# env/prod/infra — passwords for the on-box data tier.
#
# Change every value here. Each one must MATCH the one you put in the matching
# service's .env (env/prod/<svc>/.env) — the note at the bottom says which name
# goes where; keeping them in sync is the whole job.
#
# Every value in this file is a password now: object storage left this box (media
# bytes live in Cloudflare R2, and its API token belongs in env/prod/media/.env),
# so there is no access key or bucket name here to get wrong.
#
# All passwords are delivered to the services OUT-OF-BAND (PGPASSWORD /
# REDIS_PASSWORD), never embedded in a connection URL — so they may contain ANY
# characters. Generate however you like, e.g. openssl rand -base64 30.

# ── Postgres (one per service) ──
AUTH_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
USER_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
TRAVEL_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
POST_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
STORE_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
STAY_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
MESSAGE_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
MEDIA_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
NOTIFICATION_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me

# ── Redis ──
AUTH_REDIS_PASSWORD=change-me
STATS_REDIS_PASSWORD=change-me


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each service assembles its own connection URL from baked host/db + the password
# you give it — and it reads the SAME variable name as above. So "keep in sync"
# just means: put the same value under the same name in the service's .env, e.g.
#
#   env/prod/auth/.env    → AUTH_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<same as here>, AUTH_REDIS_PASSWORD=<same>
#   env/prod/media/.env   → MEDIA_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<same> (its R2 token comes
#                           from Cloudflare, not from this file)
#   env/prod/stats/.env   → STATS_REDIS_PASSWORD=<same>
#   … one line per service (see each env/prod/<svc>/.env.example).
#
# The container names + sslmode=disable are baked in the service composes; when
# you extract a DB, edit the host + sslmode on that one compose's URL line.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
